how to use git:

"git config --list" lets you check settings and whether you're loggen into any git acc rn

"git help" shows huge manual for advanced stuff

"git init" initializes a repo in ur current working directory, so make sure to cd to correct folder first

"git status" lets you check what you're currently trying to commit, don't forget to make/add to a .gitignore file

"git add" adds a file to your commit, "git add -A" adds all untracked files to your commit at once, but does respect .gitignore

"git reset" removes all files from your commit, "git reset filename" removes only that one file from your commit

"git commit -m "Message" makes a commit as configured with add/reset, as status said

"git log" shows a log of commits

"git clone URLHERE ." clones a repo from github to ur current working directory, watch ur folders

"git branch -a" shows ur branches

"git remote -v" shows ur repos

"git diff" shows you which changes you made to the repos code

"git pull origin master" lets you pull potentials changes made by other people

"git push origin branchname" or "git push -u origin branchname" lets you push your own changes onto the online repo

"git remote set-url origin git@github.com:/username/reponame.git" lets you switch to your github repo

"ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "email@adresshere" generates a ssh user key on your pc which you cna add into your github repo to allow you to push stuff to it without authentication, copy the contents of the .pub file as "key"
